```

CDN script objects use `am5` (core), `am5xy`, `am5percent`, `am5map`, `am5hierarchy`, `am5flow`, `am5radar`, `am5stock`, `am5timeline`, `am5wc`, `am5venn`, `am5gantt` namespaces.
Themes: `am5themes_Animated`, `am5themes_Dark`, etc.
Geodata: `am5geodata_worldLow`, `am5geodata_usaLow`, etc.

Where only npm CDNs are allowed (Claude artifacts and other AI sandboxes, strict CSPs), the same files are in the npm package's `dist/`: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@amcharts/amcharts5@5.23.0/dist/index.js` (or unpkg, or `node_modules/@amcharts/amcharts5/dist/`). Pin one version for every file; classic `<script>` tags, not `type="module"`. Maps beyond `dist/geodata/worldLow.js`/`usaLow.js`: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@amcharts/amcharts5-geodata@5.2.0/dist/<name>.js` (or unpkg). PDF fonts only on cdn.amcharts.com.

When bundling, keep code splitting on: with the stock toolbar's drawing/indicator controls, `<am5-chart>`, the JSON plugin or exporting, a single-file bundle inlines PDF/Excel/annotation code, about 1 MB gzipped more.

