## Settings pattern

amCharts 5 uses `.set()`, `.setAll()`, and `.get()` — not direct property assignment:

```js
// ✅ CORRECT
series.set("valueField", "value");
series.setAll({ valueField: "value", categoryField: "category" });
const val = series.get("valueField");

// ❌ WRONG
series.valueField = "value";
```

Settings are passed in the second argument of `.new()`:
```js
am5xy.LineSeries.new(root, {
  xAxis: xAxis,
  yAxis: yAxis,
  valueYField: "value",
  valueXField: "date"
})
```

## Dark theme

If the page has a dark background, always include the Dark theme. Without it, labels and grid will be invisible:

```js
root.setThemes([
  am5themes_Animated.new(root),
  am5themes_ResponsiveMax.new(root),
  am5themes_Dark.new(root)        // must come after Animated and ResponsiveMax
]);
```

**Rule:** Only add Dark theme when background is clearly dark. Default to white/light with no Dark theme unless the user asks.

## Available themes

- **Behavioral:** `Animated`, `ResponsiveMax`, `Micro` (micro charts, alone), `Responsive` (a size-based theme, which mostly hides parts)
- **ResponsiveMax on every chart:** `root.setThemes([am5themes_Animated.new(root), am5themes_ResponsiveMax.new(root)])` (`themes/ResponsiveMax.js` after `themes/Animated.js`). It fits labels and legends at any size and adapts the chart on small screens. It turns on, and each also works alone:
  - `autoLabels: true` on axis renderers: labels spaced by their size, with cut-off and overlapping ones hidden;
  - `autoLabels: true` on a `PieSeries`: the pie moves aside or shrinks, and labels wrap, shorten or hide, smallest slices first;
  - `autoLabels: true` on other series: overlapping bullet labels are hidden;
  - `keepInView: true` on axis labels (`renderer.labels.template`): a category or date period partly in view keeps its label in the part that is (unrotated labels inside their cell; with a grid step of several periods add `multiLocation: 0.5`); the theme sets it for x axis labels on charts 400 px wide or less and y axis labels on charts 400 px tall or less;
  - `autoFit: true` on a `Legend`: smaller (down to three quarters), or if that is not enough, scrolling, usually at full size; at most 30% of the chart's height above or below it;
  - `autoFit: true` on a `StockToolbar`: controls that don't fit in one row fold, first to their icons, then the period buttons into one;
  - `autoHide` on a chart's scrollbars, in px: the theme uses 400 for `scrollbarY` (chart width) and 300 for `scrollbarX` (chart height); a `scrollbarX` also hides on a chart 400 px wide or less; pinch zoom takes over;
  - `root.touchGestures = "auto"` (unless `touchGestures` or `tapToActivate` is set in code): a vertical swipe over the chart scrolls the page, a sideways or two-finger swipe works the chart. So don't set `root.tapToActivate` (`true` is `"tap"`: the page until the chart is tapped). `"chart"`, the default without the theme, gives the chart every gesture.

  When the chart's div is 400 px or less in either direction, text is at 85%. A stock chart 400 px wide or less gets less padding. A Gantt chart 600 px wide or less drops its expand, collapse and color buttons; its scrollbars hide at 500 px wide or less, the horizontal one also at 400 px tall or less. A setting set in code wins over the theme.
- **Light palettes:** `Dataviz`, `Frozen`, `Kelly`, `Material`, `Moonrise`, `Spirited`, `Ember`, `Nord`, `Pastel`, `Petroleum`, `Savanna`, `Colorblind` (Okabe-Ito, color-blindness safe), `Patterns` (pattern fills instead of flat colors)
- **Dark:** `Dark`, `Midnight`, plus dark variants of most palettes — `DatavizDark`, `FrozenDark`, `KellyDark`, `MaterialDark`, `MoonriseDark`, `SpiritedDark`, `NordDark`, `PastelDark`, `ColorblindDark`, `PatternsDark`

Palette themes are additive — put them after `Animated` and `ResponsiveMax`. The `*Dark` variants already carry dark interface colors, so do NOT also add `Dark`.

**Parameterized themes** — `Monochrome` and `Adaptive` generate a palette from colors you pass in. They are **factory functions**, not classes:

```js
import am5themes_Monochrome from "@amcharts/amcharts5/themes/Monochrome";
import am5themes_Adaptive from "@amcharts/amcharts5/themes/Adaptive";

// Single-hue lightness ramp, optional accent on the first series
root.setThemes([
  am5themes_Animated.new(root),
  am5themes_ResponsiveMax.new(root),
  am5themes_Monochrome(root, { color: 0x2c6e91, accent: 0xff7f0e, count: 7, dark: false })
]);

// Full palette generated from one or two base colors (first color IS baseColor, unless keepContrast has to move it)
root.setThemes([
  am5themes_Animated.new(root),
  am5themes_ResponsiveMax.new(root),
  am5themes_Adaptive(root, { baseColor: 0x2c6e91, baseColor2: 0xffdd00, count: 10, dark: false })
]);
```

Both handle dark mode via `dark: true` — do not also add the `Dark` theme.

## Colors — use defaults, don't invent palettes

amCharts assigns colors automatically. Do NOT create custom color palettes unless the user explicitly requests specific colors.

```js
// Get default colors programmatically
var colors = chart.get("colors");       // XY, radar, etc.
var colors = series.get("colors");      // pie/percent charts

colors.getIndex(0);   // color by index (no counter advance)
colors.next();        // next color in sequence (advances counter)
colors.reset();       // restart counter

// Only if user requests custom colors:
colors.set("colors", [am5.color(0x095256), am5.color(0x087f8c)]);
```

A scale through several colors: `am5.Color.interpolateColors(position, [ic.get("negative"), ic.get("warning"), ic.get("positive")])` with `var ic = root.interfaceColors` (`warning` is a yellow between red `negative` and green `positive`; `Color.interpolate()` between the two has a brown middle). `Adaptive`/`Monochrome` theme settings (all off by default): `interleave` (neighbouring series differ more), `mapShade` (lighter map land), `keepContrast` (`true` = 3:1 against the background, or a ratio).

3+ series in one XY chart: `chart.get("colors").set("step", 3)` or the `Colorblind` theme. Not `Dataviz`, whose first colors repeat navy and red. Lines: `strokeWidths: [2]` on the chart; `legend.markers.template.setAll({ width: 24, height: 14 })`.

Themes that reuse their list (Adaptive, Monochrome, Kelly, Material, Nord, Pastel, …, not Colorblind/Patterns/Dataviz) make each repeat round 10% lighter: `ColorSet` `repeatLightness` (HSL lightness per round, negative = darker, only with `reuse: true`). The color sets of one root share the theme's list, so whichever needs a new round first decides that round for every chart on the root. Same colors again, root-wide: `var t = am5.Theme.new(root); t.rule("ColorSet").set("repeatLightness", 0);` added last in `root.setThemes([...])`, or `repeatLightness: false` in the Adaptive/Monochrome theme settings.

## Common chart recipes

### XY chart with category axis (bar/column)
```js
const xAxis = chart.xAxes.push(am5xy.CategoryAxis.new(root, {
  categoryField: "category",
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, { minGridDistance: 30 })
}));

const yAxis = chart.yAxes.push(am5xy.ValueAxis.new(root, {
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererY.new(root, {})
}));

const series = chart.series.push(am5xy.ColumnSeries.new(root, {
  xAxis: xAxis,
  yAxis: yAxis,
  valueYField: "value",
  categoryXField: "category"
}));

xAxis.data.setAll(data);  // CategoryAxis needs data too!
series.data.setAll(data);
```

### XY chart with date axis (time series)
```js
const xAxis = chart.xAxes.push(am5xy.DateAxis.new(root, {
  baseInterval: { timeUnit: "day", count: 1 },
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, { minGridDistance: 50 })
}));

const yAxis = chart.yAxes.push(am5xy.ValueAxis.new(root, {
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererY.new(root, {})
}));

const series = chart.series.push(am5xy.LineSeries.new(root, {
  xAxis: xAxis,
  yAxis: yAxis,
  valueYField: "value",
  valueXField: "date"
}));

// Date values must be timestamps (milliseconds)
series.data.setAll([
  { date: new Date(2024, 0, 1).getTime(), value: 100 },
  { date: new Date(2024, 1, 1).getTime(), value: 120 }
]);
```

### Pie / Donut chart
```js
const chart = root.container.children.push(
  am5percent.PieChart.new(root, {
    innerRadius: am5.percent(50),  // 0 for pie, >0 for donut
    layout: root.verticalLayout
  })
);

const series = chart.series.push(am5percent.PieSeries.new(root, {
  valueField: "value",
  categoryField: "category"
}));

series.data.setAll([
  { category: "A", value: 10 },
  { category: "B", value: 7 },
  { category: "C", value: 3 }
]);
```

### Map chart (choropleth)
```js
const chart = root.container.children.push(
  am5map.MapChart.new(root, {
    panX: "rotateX",
    projection: am5map.geoMercator()
  })
);

const polygonSeries = chart.series.push(am5map.MapPolygonSeries.new(root, {
  geoJSON: am5geodata_worldLow,
  valueField: "value",
  calculateAggregates: true
}));
```

### Map Sankey (geographic flow bands)
```js
// Requires: map package + geodata (NOT flow package)
var polygonSeries = chart.series.push(am5map.MapPolygonSeries.new(root, {
  geoJSON: am5geodata_worldLow
}));
var sankeySeries = chart.series.push(am5map.MapSankeySeries.new(root, {
  polygonSeries: polygonSeries,  // required: resolves country IDs to centroids
  maxWidth: 5                    // max band width in geographic degrees
}));
sankeySeries.mapPolygons.template.setAll({
  fillOpacity: 0.5, strokeOpacity: 0,
  tooltipText: "{sourceId} > {targetId}: {value}"
});
// MapSankeySeries auto-resolves sourceId/targetId once polygonSeries is ready —
// set data directly, no datavalidated wrapper needed.
sankeySeries.data.setAll([
  { sourceId: "BR", targetId: "DE", value: 350 },
  { sourceId: "CN", targetId: "US", value: 600 }
]);
// Alternative: use explicit coordinates (skips centroid lookup entirely):
// { sourceLongitude: 2.35, sourceLatitude: 48.86, targetLongitude: -74.01, targetLatitude: 40.71, value: 100 }
```

### Funnel chart
```js
const chart = root.container.children.push(
  am5percent.SlicedChart.new(root, { layout: root.verticalLayout })
);

const series = chart.series.push(am5percent.FunnelSeries.new(root, {
  name: "Funnel",
  valueField: "value",
  categoryField: "stage",
  orientation: "vertical",
  bottomRatio: 0   // 0 = rectangles (default), 1 = each slice narrows to the next (trapezoids)
}));

series.data.setAll([
  { stage: "Visits", value: 10000 },
  { stage: "Signups", value: 5200 },
  { stage: "Paid", value: 1400 }
]);
```

### Stock chart (candlestick with toolbar)
```js
// Requires: index.js, xy.js, stock.js
// HTML: <div id="chartcontrols"></div> <div id="chartdiv"></div>
root.numberFormatter.set("numberFormat", "#,###.00##"); // prices: cents, and up to 4 decimals for small ones
const stockChart = root.container.children.push(
  am5stock.StockChart.new(root, {})
);

const mainPanel = stockChart.panels.push(
  am5stock.StockPanel.new(root, { wheelY: "zoomX", panX: true, panY: true })
);

const dateAxis = mainPanel.xAxes.push(am5xy.DateAxis.new(root, {
  baseInterval: { timeUnit: "day", count: 1 },
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {})
}));

const valueAxis = mainPanel.yAxes.push(am5xy.ValueAxis.new(root, {
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererY.new(root, {}),
  tooltip: am5.Tooltip.new(root, {}),
  preferredDecimals: [0, 2]  // labels: whole numbers, or cents
}));

const valueSeries = mainPanel.series.push(am5xy.CandlestickSeries.new(root, {
  name: "STCK",
  xAxis: dateAxis, yAxis: valueAxis,
  valueXField: "Date", valueYField: "Close",
  highValueYField: "High", lowValueYField: "Low",
  openValueYField: "Open", calculateAggregates: true
}));

stockChart.set("stockSeries", valueSeries);  // CRITICAL: register main series
valueSeries.data.setAll(data);
```

### Serpentine timeline
```js
const chart = root.container.children.push(am5timeline.SerpentineChart.new(root, {
  orientation: "vertical", levelCount: 3,
  yAxisRadius: am5.percent(50) // Percent; no yAxisInnerRadius setting exists
}));
const yRenderer = am5timeline.AxisRendererCurveY.new(root, {}); // create Y renderer FIRST
const xAxis = chart.xAxes.push(am5xy.DateAxis.new(root, {
  baseInterval: { timeUnit: "day", count: 1 },
  renderer: am5timeline.AxisRendererCurveX.new(root, { yRenderer: yRenderer }) // NOT AxisRendererX
}));
const yAxis = chart.yAxes.push(am5xy.ValueAxis.new(root, {
  renderer: yRenderer // reuse the same renderer
}));
const series = chart.series.push(am5timeline.CurveLineSeries.new(root, { // NOT LineSeries
  xAxis, yAxis, valueYField: "value", valueXField: "date"
}));
series.data.setAll(data); // timestamps for DateAxis
```

