### Venn diagram
```js
// Requires: index.js, venn.js
// NOTE: There is NO VennDiagram class — push Venn directly into a Container
const container = root.container.children.push(am5.Container.new(root, {
  width: am5.percent(100),
  height: am5.percent(100),
  layout: root.verticalLayout
}));

const series = container.children.push(am5venn.Venn.new(root, {
  categoryField: "name",
  valueField: "value",
  intersectionsField: "sets"
}));

series.data.setAll([
  { name: "A", value: 100 },
  { name: "B", value: 80 },
  { name: "A∩B", value: 30, sets: ["A", "B"] }
]);
```

### Gantt chart
```js
// Requires: index.js, xy.js, plugins/colorPicker.js, gantt.js
const chart = root.container.children.push(am5gantt.Gantt.new(root, {
  editable: true,
  durationUnit: "day"
}));

// Gantt uses TWO separate data calls — NOT nested children
chart.yAxis.data.setAll([
  { id: "phase1", name: "Phase 1", color: am5.color(0x297373) },
  { id: "taskA", name: "Task A", parentId: "phase1" },
  { id: "taskB", name: "Task B", parentId: "phase1" }
]);
chart.series.data.setAll([
  { id: "phase1", start: new Date(2024, 0, 1).getTime(), duration: 10, progress: 1 },
  { id: "taskA", start: new Date(2024, 0, 1).getTime(), duration: 5, progress: 1 },
  { id: "taskB", start: new Date(2024, 0, 6).getTime(), duration: 5, progress: 0.8 }
]);
```

## Events

```js
// Click on elements
series.columns.template.events.on("click", function(ev) {
  console.log("Clicked:", ev.target.dataItem.dataContext);
});

// Lifecycle
series.events.on("datavalidated", function() { /* data ready */ });

// One-time listener
series.events.once("datavalidated", function() { /* runs once */ });

// Setting change watch
sprite.on("width", function(width) { console.log("Width:", width); });

// Remove listener
var disposer = sprite.events.on("click", handler);
disposer.dispose();

// Common events: click, pointerover, pointerout, pointerdown, globalpointermove
```

To open a link on click, no handler is needed: `series.set("urlField", "url")` makes each item's bullet, column, slice, Venn slice, map polygon or map line open the URL from its data row (`linkTarget`, default `"_self"`). Hierarchy nodes, flow nodes/links and word-cloud labels are not linked — use a `click` handler there.

On touch, a tap on a pannable chart (`panX`/`panY`), under a zoom/select cursor or on a `draggable` sprite fires no DOM `click`; amCharts' `events.on("click")` still fires.

## Adapters

Dynamically modify a setting value before it's applied:

```js
series.columns.template.adapters.add("fill", function(fill, target) {
  return target.dataItem.get("valueY") > 100
    ? am5.color(0x00cc00)
    : am5.color(0xcc0000);
});
```

## States

```js
series.columns.template.states.create("hover", {
  fillOpacity: 0.8,
  scale: 1.05
});
// Built-in states: "hover", "active", "disabled", "hidden"
```

Once a state has changed a setting, the `"default"` state keeps the value from before and restores it on every unhover. To change such a setting later, change it in both places: `sprite.set("fill", c); sprite.states.lookup("default")?.set("fill", c);`.

`sprite.hover()` also shows its tooltip; to highlight other sprites from an event use `sprite.states.applyAnimate("hover")` / `"default"`, or the shared tooltip jumps to the last one.

## Heat rules

Color or size elements by data value. Requires `calculateAggregates: true` on the series (unless `minValue`/`maxValue` are set). Values outside `minValue` / `maxValue` get `min` / `max`. `logarithmic: true` spreads values on a log scale; zero and below get `min`.

```js
// Color columns by value
series.set("heatRules", [{
  target: series.columns.template,
  dataField: "valueY",
  min: am5.color(0xe5dc36),
  max: am5.color(0x5faa46),
  key: "fill"
}]);

// Scale bullet radius by value — bullets need am5.Template
var circleTemplate = am5.Template.new({});
series.bullets.push(function(root, series, dataItem) {
  return am5.Bullet.new(root, {
    sprite: am5.Circle.new(root, {
      fill: series.get("fill")
    }, circleTemplate)              // template as 3rd arg
  });
});
series.set("heatRules", [{
  target: circleTemplate,
  dataField: "valueY",
  min: 3, max: 25,
  key: "radius"
}]);
```

**Heat rule keys:** `"fill"`, `"radius"`, `"opacity"`, `"strokeWidth"`, `"fontSize"`, etc.
**customFunction:** `(sprite, min, max, value)` for full control.
**stops:** `stops: [ic.get("negative"), ic.get("warning"), ic.get("positive")]` (with `var ic = root.interfaceColors`) in place of `min`/`max` for a scale through more than two values (numbers, percents or colors); `HeatLegend` takes the same list as `colors` in place of `startColor`/`endColor`.

**HeatLegend:**
```js
var heatLegend = chart.children.push(am5.HeatLegend.new(root, {
  orientation: "horizontal",
  startColor: am5.color(0xe5dc36),
  endColor: am5.color(0x5faa46),
  stepCount: 5
}));
series.events.on("datavalidated", function() {   // the end labels show these numbers
  heatLegend.set("startValue", series.getPrivate("valueLow"));
  heatLegend.set("endValue", series.getPrivate("valueHigh"));
});
```

`startText`/`endText` replace the end numbers (`""` hides them; `{startValue}` in them isn't filled in).

## Accessibility

```js
series.columns.template.setAll({
  focusable: true,
  ariaLabel: "{categoryX}: {valueY}",
  role: "figure"
});
// Keyboard: TAB to navigate focusable elements, ENTER to click
// focusableGroup: "series1" — TAB to first, arrows within group
```

Windows High Contrast: interface colors (labels, grid, axes, buttons) follow the system colors by default; `am5.Root.new("chartdiv", { forcedColors: false })` opts out. `am5.Modal` takes an `ariaLabel` (dialog name); `ariaExpanded` is an element setting.

## Container & Layout

```js
var container = root.container.children.push(am5.Container.new(root, {
  width: am5.percent(100),
  height: am5.percent(100),
  layout: root.verticalLayout  // also: horizontalLayout, gridLayout
}));
container.setAll({ paddingTop: 10, paddingBottom: 10, marginLeft: 20 });
```

**Layout options:**

| Layout | Access | Behavior |
|--------|--------|----------|
| Vertical | `root.verticalLayout` | Children stacked top-to-bottom |
| Horizontal | `root.horizontalLayout` | Children in a row left-to-right |
| Grid | `root.gridLayout` | Multi-column grid |
| Custom grid | `am5.GridLayout.new(root, { maxColumns: 3 })` | Grid with custom column count |
| None | omit `layout` | Children placed at x/y coordinates |

## UI Elements

amCharts 5 provides built-in interactive UI widgets. **Prefer these over HTML elements** when building controls.

| Element | Class | Description |
|---------|-------|-------------|
| Button | `am5.Button` | Clickable with label, icon, hover/down/active states |
| Slider | `am5.Slider` | Single-value slider (0-1 range), fires `rangechanged` |
| Scrollbar | `am5.Scrollbar` | Two-grip range selector |
| NumericStepper | `am5.NumericStepper` | Number input with up/down arrows |
| ProgressPie | `am5.ProgressPie` | Circular progress indicator |
| SpriteResizer | `am5.SpriteResizer` | Drag-to-resize handles on any sprite |
| EditableLabel | `am5.EditableLabel` | Label editable on click |
| Modal | `am5.Modal` | HTML overlay dialog with `open()`/`close()` |

```js
// Slider controlling a chart value
var slider = container.children.push(am5.Slider.new(root, {
  orientation: "horizontal",
  start: 0.5,
  width: am5.percent(80),
  centerX: am5.percent(50),
  x: am5.percent(50)
}));
slider.events.on("rangechanged", function(ev) {
  var value = ev.start;  // 0-1 range
});

// Button
var button = container.children.push(am5.Button.new(root, {
  label: am5.Label.new(root, { text: "Reset" }),
  centerX: am5.percent(50),
  x: am5.percent(50)
}));
button.events.on("click", function() {
  slider.set("start", 0.5);
});
```

## Dynamic data

```js
series.data.setAll(newData);              // replace all (NO animation)
series.data.push({ cat: "X", val: 1 });  // add
series.data.setIndex(0, newItem);         // update at index (ANIMATES)
series.data.removeIndex(2);               // remove at index
series.data.insertIndex(1, newItem);      // insert at index

// To update data WITH animation, use setIndex() per item:
// newData.forEach(function(item, i) { series.data.setIndex(i, item); });

// IMPORTANT: series.dataItems is a plain array, NOT a List
// ❌ series.dataItems.each(fn)           — will throw
// ✅ series.dataItems.forEach(fn)        — standard JS
// ✅ am5.array.each(series.dataItems, function(dataItem) {})

// Changing a data item's value directly: set the WORKING key too, or nothing moves
xySeries.dataItems[0].setAll({ valueX: 4, valueY: 7, valueXWorking: 4, valueYWorking: 7 });
pieSeries.dataItems[0].setAll({ value: 80, valueWorking: 80 });   // pie/funnel: valueWorking
// dataItem.bullets is undefined until the item is drawn (not yet in datavalidated): style bullets inside the bullet function
// Maps: setIndex with a new geometry switches only when interpolationDuration ends; set it to 0 for per-frame updates
// A data item's bullets are a property: dataItem.bullets?.[0]?.get("sprite") (dataItem.get("bullets") is undefined)
```

## Performance

No zoom animation: `interpolationDuration: 0` on the X axis and the value axis (there is no `zoomAnimation`); `zoom…(a, b, 0)` jumps. Fast streams: `interpolationDuration: 0` on series and axes, plus `root.fps = 30`. Large scatter: draw all dots in one `am5.Graphics` instead of bullets, up to about 50,000 points (references/xy.md "Scatter / Bubble chart"). No "rendered" event: `datavalidated` + one `frameended` fires before drawing ends; done = two animation frames in a row with no `root` `frameended` (helper in SKILL.md "Events"). Bar chart race: no sort setting; re-sort `series.dataItems` and `yAxis.dataItems` every 100 ms with `deltaPosition` (references/xy.md, "Bar chart race").

## Data processor (for external/API data)

```js
series.data.processor = am5.DataProcessor.new(root, {
  dateFields: ["date"],
  dateFormat: "yyyy-MM-dd",   // optional: without it Date parses the strings ("2024-03-15" = midnight UTC)
  numericFields: ["value"],
  emptyAs: 0   // replaces null, undefined and "" (not 0 or false)
});
// Configure BEFORE setting data
```

