## Key differences from amCharts 4 (common AI mistakes)

| amCharts 4 (WRONG) | amCharts 5 (CORRECT) |
|---------------------|----------------------|
| `am4core.create("div", am4charts.XYChart)` | `am5.Root.new("div")` then `am5xy.XYChart.new(root, {})` |
| `new am4charts.CategoryAxis()` | `am5xy.CategoryAxis.new(root, { ... })` |
| `chart.data = [...]` | `series.data.setAll([...])` |
| `series.dataFields.valueY = "v"` | `valueYField: "v"` in `.new()` settings |
| `am4core.color("#f00")` | `am5.color(0xff0000)` or `am5.color("#f00")` |
| `new am4charts.Legend()` | `am5.Legend.new(root, {})` |
| `chart.cursor = new am4charts.XYCursor()` | `chart.set("cursor", am5xy.XYCursor.new(root, {}))` |
| SVG-based rendering | Canvas by default; SVG optional (`renderer: am5.SVGRenderer`) |
| `am4core.useTheme(am4themes_animated)` | `root.setThemes([am5themes_Animated.new(root), am5themes_ResponsiveMax.new(root)])` |

## Common pitfalls

1. **CategoryAxis needs data too** — Unlike ValueAxis, CategoryAxis must receive data: `xAxis.data.setAll(data)` in addition to `series.data.setAll(data)`.

2. **Date values must be timestamps** — DateAxis expects numbers (ms since epoch), not Date objects or strings. Use `new Date(...).getTime()`.

3. **Renderer is required for every axis** — Always pass a `renderer` when creating an axis: `am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {})`.

4. **Don't forget `root` in `.new()` calls** — Every `.new()` call (except Root itself) takes `root` as the first arg.

5. **Dispose via root** — To clean up, call `root.dispose()`, not `chart.dispose()`.

6. **Colors** — Use `am5.color(0xFF0000)` or `am5.color("#ff0000")`. For color sets, access `chart.get("colors")`.

7. **Percent values** — Use `am5.percent(50)` not plain `50` or `"50%"` when a setting expects a Percent value.

8. **children.push()** — Adding elements to containers uses `.children.push()` which returns the element. Always capture the return value.

9. **No CSS styling** — amCharts 5 draws on canvas by default, so CSS cannot reach chart elements; even with `am5.SVGRenderer` the shapes have no per-element classes, are rewritten on redraw, and exports ignore page CSS. Use themes or `.set()`/`.setAll()`.

10. **Hierarchy charts are chart-less** — Treemap, force-directed, etc. add series directly to `root.container` (or a wrapper Container), not to a chart object.

11. **`dataItems` is a plain array** — `series.dataItems` does NOT have `.each()`. Use `series.dataItems.forEach(fn)` or `am5.array.each(series.dataItems, fn)`. Only `series.data` (the ListData object) has `.each()`.

12. **CDN script load order matters** — `index.js` must load first, then `xy.js`, then any package that depends on it (`radar.js`, `timeline.js`, `gantt.js`). Wrong order causes runtime errors. Correct order: `index.js` > `xy.js` > `radar.js` / `timeline.js` / `gantt.js` > `themes/*.js`. Gantt also needs `plugins/colorPicker.js` before `gantt.js`. From an npm CDN, the same order under `…/@amcharts/amcharts5@<version>/dist/`, every file from one pinned version.

13. **No `minorGrid` / `minorTicks` / `minorLabels` objects** — These properties don't exist. Enable minor grid via renderer flags:
```js
am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {
  minorGridEnabled: true,    // shows minor grid lines
  minorLabelsEnabled: true   // optional: shows minor labels
})
```
Style minor elements through theme rules targeting the `"minor"` tag — they auto-inherit main grid appearance but slightly lighter.

14. **Flow chart animated bullets go on `series.bullets`, NOT `series.links.template.bullets`** — To animate labels/circles flowing along Sankey/Chord links, use `series.bullets.push()`. Animate `bullet.locationX` (Sankey) or `bullet.locationY` (Chord) from 0>1 with `loops: Infinity`. Use an adapter on opacity based on position for fade effect:
```js
// Sankey: use locationX. For Chord: replace ALL locationX with locationY.
series.bullets.push(function(root, series, dataItem) {
  var label = am5.Label.new(root, {
    text: "${value}B", populateText: true,
    centerX: am5.p50, fill: am5.color(0xffffff)
  });
  var bullet = am5.Bullet.new(root, {
    locationX: 0, sprite: label, autoRotate: true
  });
  bullet.animate({
    key: "locationX", from: 0, to: 1,
    duration: Math.random() * 10000 + 2000, loops: Infinity
  });
  label.adapters.add("opacity", function(opacity) {
    return 0.5 - Math.abs(0.5 - bullet.get("locationX"));
  });
  bullet.on("locationX", function() {
    label.set("opacity", label.get("opacity"));
  });
  return bullet;
});
```

15. **`MapPointSeries` needs `latitudeField`/`longitudeField` unless your data fields are named exactly `latitude`/`longitude`** — those are the defaults, so matching data works undeclared. Any other naming silently renders nothing:
```js
// FINE — data uses "latitude"/"longitude", which are the defaults
am5map.MapPointSeries.new(root, {})

// WRONG — data uses lat/lng, points won't show
am5map.MapPointSeries.new(root, {})

// CORRECT — tell the series which fields hold coordinates
am5map.MapPointSeries.new(root, {
  latitudeField: "lat",
  longitudeField: "lng"
})
```
Neither is needed when using `pushDataItem({ latitude: ..., longitude: ... })`, which passes coordinates directly to the data item.

16. **`data.setAll()` does NOT animate — use `data.setIndex()` for animated updates** — `series.data.setAll(newData)` replaces everything instantly with no transition. To update data with smooth animation, use `series.data.setIndex(i, newItem)` per item:
```js
// WRONG — no animation
series.data.setAll(newData);

// CORRECT — animates each value change
newData.forEach(function(item, i) {
  series.data.setIndex(i, item);
});
```

17. **`color.lighten()` / `color.darken()` are NOT instance methods** — `am5.color(0xff0000).lighten(0.3)` does NOT work. Use static methods: `am5.Color.lighten(color, 0.3)` to lighten, `am5.Color.lighten(color, -0.3)` to darken. There is NO `darken()` method — use negative lighten. Also: `am5.Color.brighten()`, `am5.Color.saturate()`.

18. **Venn diagram has no `VennDiagram` class** — `am5venn.Venn` is pushed directly into a `Container`, NOT into a chart's `series`. See references/venn.md.

19. **Timeline `AxisRendererCurveX` requires `yRenderer`** — Always create the Y renderer first, then pass it:
```js
var yRenderer = am5timeline.AxisRendererCurveY.new(root, {});
var xRenderer = am5timeline.AxisRendererCurveX.new(root, {
  yRenderer: yRenderer
});
```
Without this, crashes with `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'axis')`.

20. **Gantt data uses TWO separate calls** — Do NOT use `chart.data.setAll()`. Set categories on `chart.yAxis.data.setAll([{id, name, parentId, color}])` and tasks on `chart.series.data.setAll([{id, start, duration, progress, linkTo}])`. Use flat `parentId` for hierarchy, NOT nested `children` arrays. CDN order: `index.js` > `xy.js` > `plugins/colorPicker.js` > `gantt.js` > `themes/Animated.js`:
```js
// WRONG — single data call with nested children
chart.data.setAll([{ name: "Task", children: [...] }]);

// CORRECT — two separate calls with flat parentId hierarchy
chart.yAxis.data.setAll([
  { id: "phase1", name: "Phase 1", color: am5.color(0x297373) },
  { id: "task1", name: "Task 1", parentId: "phase1" }
]);
chart.series.data.setAll([
  { id: "phase1", start: timestamp, duration: 10, progress: 0.5 },
  { id: "task1", start: timestamp, duration: 5, progress: 1, linkTo: ["phase1"] }
]);
```

21. **No continent-level geodata at top-level CDN** — `geodata/europeLow.js` does NOT exist. Use `geodata/region/world/europeLow.js` (global: `am5geodata_region_world_europeLow`) or filter `worldLow` with `include: ["FR", "DE", "ES", ...]`. On jsDelivr or unpkg: `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@amcharts/amcharts5-geodata@<version>/dist/region/world/europeLow.js`.

22. **Do not add chart titles as HTML** — HTML titles are outside the chart and won't appear in exports. Use `am5.Label` pushed into the container BEFORE the chart, with `verticalLayout` on the container. See "Chart title" in Common components above.

23. **`XYChartScrollbar` has no `xAxis`/`yAxis` settings; its axes live in `scrollbar.chart`** — the preview is a chart of its own. Push its axes into `scrollbar.chart.xAxes`/`yAxes` and its series into `scrollbar.chart.series`, and give that series the data. Axes passed to `XYChartScrollbar.new()` are never added to the preview (its series then throws), and `get("xAxis")` only hands back whatever you passed:
```js
// CORRECT — the scrollbar's preview chart gets its own axes and series
var scrollbar = chart.set("scrollbarX", am5xy.XYChartScrollbar.new(root, {
  orientation: "horizontal",
  height: 50
}));
var sbxAxis = scrollbar.chart.xAxes.push(am5xy.DateAxis.new(root, {
  baseInterval: { timeUnit: "day", count: 1 },
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererX.new(root, {})
}));
var sbyAxis = scrollbar.chart.yAxes.push(am5xy.ValueAxis.new(root, {
  renderer: am5xy.AxisRendererY.new(root, {})
}));
var sbSeries = scrollbar.chart.series.push(am5xy.LineSeries.new(root, {
  xAxis: sbxAxis, yAxis: sbyAxis, valueYField: "value", valueXField: "date"
}));
sbSeries.data.setAll(data);   // the preview series needs the data too
```

24. **`am5.color()` only accepts hex integers or CSS strings** — `am5.color(0xff0000)`, `am5.color("#ff0000")`, `am5.color("rgb(255,0,0)")` are valid. `am5.color({ r: 255, g: 0, b: 0 })` is NOT — it throws.

25. **`MapChart` has no default `colors`** — the setting exists (inherited from `SerialChart`), but nothing sets it on a map, so `chart.get("colors")` returns `undefined`, and map series don't use it anyway. XY and Radar charts (and percent series, via `series.get("colors")`) get a ColorSet from the theme. For maps, make your own: `am5.ColorSet.new(root, {})`.

26. **`VoronoiTreemap` has NO `.rectangles` property** — Unlike `Treemap` (which has `series.rectangles.template`), `VoronoiTreemap` renders organic polygon cells. Style via `series.nodes.template` and its children, not `.rectangles`.
27. **Labels with data placeholders need `populateText: true`** — `Label` defaults to `populateText: false`; labels the library makes for you (axis, legend, tooltip, pie/funnel slice labels, hierarchy and flow node labels…) get `true` from their own theme rules, but a `Label` you create does not. Any Label you create whose `text` has `{placeholders}` (a bullet sprite, a child of a bullet's container, a map point label) needs `populateText: true`, or it shows the braces literally. Example: `am5.Label.new(root, { text: "{name}", populateText: true, ... })`. A `tooltipText` is filled in regardless.
28. **Globe rotation uses negative coordinates** — To center the globe (`geoOrthographic`) on a geographic point, set `rotationX` to **-longitude** and `rotationY` to **-latitude**. E.g., to center on Paris (48.86°N, 2.35°E): `chart.animate({ key: "rotationX", to: -2.35 }); chart.animate({ key: "rotationY", to: -48.86 });`. Using positive values rotates the globe the wrong way.
29. **`positionOnLine` with multi-segment lines limits per-segment control** — `MapPointSeries` data items can animate along a line via `positionOnLine` (0>1). If the line has 3+ points (multi-segment), position 0.5 is the midpoint of the *entire* path, making per-segment effects (scaling at each segment midpoint, pausing between segments, etc.) difficult. For advanced per-segment animations, use **single-segment lines** (2 points each) and animate the bullet across them sequentially. A point on a line can be a plain data row — `{ lineId: "jfk-lhr", positionOnLine: 0, autoRotate: true }` (the line's data `id`) — instead of `pushDataItem({ lineDataItem })`; data rows are serialized, pushed data items are not. A looping flight can be declared on the bullet sprite: `animations: [{ target: "dataItem", key: "positionOnLine", from: 0, to: 1, duration: 6000, loops: 0, yoyo: true }]` — with `autoRotate` the point then turns round on the way back (a point moved by `dataItem.animate()` in code is not flipped).
30. **`MapSankeySeries` is in the map package, NOT the flow package** — Geographic Sankey bands on a map use `am5map.MapSankeySeries` from `@amcharts/amcharts5/map`. Do NOT import `@amcharts/amcharts5/flow` for this. It requires a `polygonSeries` setting pointing to a `MapPolygonSeries` to resolve country IDs to centroids. Data uses `{ sourceId, targetId, value }` with ISO alpha-2 country codes. Bands are styled via `sankeySeries.mapPolygons.template`, nodes via `sankeySeries.nodes.mapPolygons.template`. Supports waypoints, explicit lat/long coordinates, multi-level flows, and animated bullets via `locationX`. Data can be set directly (e.g. `sankeySeries.data.setAll([...])`) at any time — `MapSankeySeries` auto-resolves `sourceId`/`targetId` once the referenced `polygonSeries` finishes loading, so no `datavalidated` wrapper is needed. **Never** call `polygonSeries.data.setAll()` with custom objects — this replaces geoJSON-derived data items and breaks centroid resolution.

31. **Do NOT exclude Antarctica (`exclude: ["AQ"]`) by default** — Many amCharts demos exclude Antarctica because they use Mercator projection where it appears disproportionately large. This is a demo-specific choice, not a best practice. Unless the user explicitly asks to exclude Antarctica, or references a demo that does so, keep Antarctica in the map. With non-Mercator projections (`geoNaturalEarth1`, `geoEqualEarth`, `geoOrthographic`, `geoEquirectangular`), Antarctica renders at a reasonable size.

32. **Custom GeoJSON for `MapPolygonSeries` needs CLOCKWISE exterior rings** — the RFC 7946 counter-clockwise default is read by the spherical projection as "the globe minus the polygon", so every polygon floods the whole map. amCharts does not rewind; reverse each polygon whose `am5map.getGeoArea({ type: "Polygon", coordinates: poly }) > 2 * Math.PI` (`poly.forEach(r => r.reverse())`): safe on clockwise data, and it catches rings flipped by simplifying. To fit a custom region use `chart.zoomToGeoBounds({ left, right, top, bottom }, duration)` (left/right = longitude, top/bottom = latitude).

33. **`axis.dispose()` does NOT remove the axis from `chart.xAxes`/`yAxes`** — use `chart.yAxes.removeValue(axis)` / `removeIndex(i)` (the list disposes it). `series.dispose()` does self-remove from `chart.series`; axes are the exception.

34. **Declare bullet callbacks as `function(root, series, dataItem)`** — closing over an outer `root` breaks JSON round-trips through `ChartSerializer`.

35. **Tooltips on non-XY charts need no `am5.Tooltip` instance** — just `tooltipText` on the right template (`slices.template`, `nodes.template`, flow `nodes.nodes.template` / `links.template`, wordcloud `labels.template`, `mapPolygons.template`); the root's shared tooltip (`root.container.get("tooltip")`) is used. Create a `Tooltip` only when it must look different, or on XY charts where series/axis tooltips are cursor-driven. Heat rules on bullets: `target` must be the `am5.Template` the sprite is built from, `dataField` is the property key (`"valueY"`, not the column name), and `calculateAggregates: true` is required — otherwise every bullet silently gets the same size.

36. **Serialize the chart's top container child** (`serializer.serializeAll(root.container.children.getIndex(0))` — the chart, or the series on chart-less types). A series straight in `root.container` or one with `selectedDataItem` set serializes too (a drilled-down hierarchy selection is not restored). `ChartSerializer` does not capture adapters, Venn `hoverGraphics`, a `ZoomTools` you added to a hand-made `ZoomableContainer` (use `am5.SerialChartContainer`), or data items added with `pushDataItem()` — re-apply those after `JsonParser.parse()`. It does save user `themeTags`, declared `animations`, endless code-started loops (`loops: Infinity`, named easing) as `animations` entries (`runningAnimations`, default `true`), a data-item loop started in code (on the bullet sprite; loops that differ per item go in each data row), hidden series, elements added to plot/axis containers, a `ZoomableContainer`'s `contents`, `Date` values, and `root.interfaceColors` colors as `"@root.interfaceColors.get('…')"` references (palette colors as `"@colors.getIndex(n)"`). Prefer a declared `animations` entry over `animate()` for effects that must survive JSON; for the opening animation use `autoAppear: true`.

37. **Several colors in one `am5.Graphics` `draw`:** call `display.beginPath()` before each color (`endFill()` fills everything since the last `beginPath()`), and give the Graphics no `fill` of its own (after `draw` it fills the current path again, so the last shape takes that `fill`). An own stroke re-strokes the last path too.

38. **XY live updates and zooming:** `zoomToValues()` right after `axis.setAll({ min, max })` uses the old range; call `axis.zoom((v0 - min) / (max - min), (v1 - min) / (max - min))` instead, or wait a frame. `maxZoomFactor` is an axis setting, not an `XYChart` one. A Label inside a Container bullet keeps its first text (`{valueXWorking}` won't count along with `dataItem.animate()`) unless the `Bullet` has `dynamic: true`.

39. **Map zoom and home:** `zoomStep` (default `2`) multiplies/divides `zoomLevel` for the buttons, `zoomIn()`/`zoomOut()`, the wheel (one step per wheel event) and double clicks, so use `1.1`–`1.2` for fine control; `wheelSensitivity` affects only wheel rotation. On a globe (`panX: "rotateX"`), `goHome()` restores rotation only from `homeRotationX`/`homeRotationY` (−longitude/−latitude), not from `homeGeoPoint`. With `autoHome: true` and no `homeZoomLevel`, home zoom is 1, so set `homeZoomLevel` to the starting `zoomLevel`. US congressional districts are packs under `geodata/region/usa/<pack>/` (`congressional`, `congressional2022`, `congressional2025`, `congressional120`), e.g. global `am5geodata_region_usa_congressional120_usaCongressionalLow`; there is no top-level `geodata/usaCongressionalLow.js`.

40. **`am5.Graphics` redraws only when `draw` changes:** set a new closure each update, not the same function.

41. **`templateField` goes on the template** (`series.columns.template.set("templateField", "columnSettings")`, likewise `mapPolygons.template`), not on the series.

42. **Legend value without a cursor:** `legendValueText` shows only under a cursor; otherwise the value label uses `legendRangeValueText`, where `{valueY}` is empty and `{valueYClose}`/`{valueYSum}`/`{valueYHigh}`… need `calculateAggregates: true` on the series (empty, no warning).

43. **Number formats:** with no `.` the decimals stay (`'#,###'` → `6,708.044`; only floating-point noise is dropped); `'#,###.'` gives whole numbers, `'#,###.00'` two decimals. Number placeholders get thousands separators (`{year}` → `2,024`; use `{year.formatNumber('#')}`). Positive|negative|zero sections use `|`, not `;`; the negative part keeps its minus unless it has the `s` modifier (`#,###|(#,###s)|'-'`); `#,###s` keeps its thousands separator. Prices: `root.numberFormatter.set("numberFormat", "#,###.00##")`, and `preferredDecimals: [0, 2]` on the price `ValueAxis` for labels in whole numbers or cents.

## Frameworks (React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, React Native)

In a framework app, use amCharts' package for it (react 5.0.1, vue 5.0.2, angular 5.0.1, svelte 5.0.3, react-native 5.0.4, which loads 5.23.0; the web ones need amCharts 5.21.4+) instead of hand-written mount/dispose code. It makes the chart when its element is there, disposes it with the component, and loads the library in the browser only, so server rendering works (Next.js, Nuxt, SvelteKit, Angular SSR). Install it with the library: `npm install @amcharts/amcharts5 @amcharts/amcharts5-react`.

| Framework | Package | A chart in code | A chart from a JSON config |
|---|---|---|---|
| React 18+ | `@amcharts/amcharts5-react` | `const { ref, root, result } = useAmChart((root) => { … }, [data])` + `<div ref={ref} style={{ height: "500px" }} />` | `<AmChart config={config} themes={[am5themes_Animated, am5themes_ResponsiveMax]} />` |
| Vue 3.5.2+ | `@amcharts/amcharts5-vue` | `const { root, result } = useAmChart(useTemplateRef("chart"), (root) => { … }, { watch: () => props.data })` (shallow refs) | `<AmChart :config="config" :themes="themes" @ready="…" />` |
| Angular 19+ | `@amcharts/amcharts5-angular` | `AmChartDirective`: `<div [amChart]="buildChart" [amChartDeps]="[data()]" (amChartReady)="…">`, `buildChart = (root: Root) => { … }` (arrow-function property) | `AmChartComponent`: `<am5-chart [config]="config" [themes]="themes" (amChartReady)="…">` |
| Svelte 4+ | `@amcharts/amcharts5-svelte` | Svelte 5.29+: `<div {@attach attachAmChart(buildChart)}>`; older: `<div use:amChart={{ setup: buildChart, deps: [data] }}>` | `{@attach attachAmChartConfig({ config, themes })}` or `use:amChartConfig={{ config }}` on `<am5-chart>` |
| React Native 0.72+ | `@amcharts/amcharts5-react-native` + `react-native-webview` 13+ | `<AmChart code={codeString} data={data} />` | `<AmChart config={config} themes={["Animated", "ResponsiveMax"]} />` |

```jsx
// React (Vue, Angular and Svelte work the same way: the function gets the root)
const { ref, result } = useAmChart((root) => {
  const chart = root.container.children.push(am5xy.XYChart.new(root, {}));
  // ... axes and series, as in any example, after its Root.new() line
  return { xAxis, series };
}, []); // [data] would make the chart again on every change

useEffect(() => {
  if (result) { result.xAxis.data.setAll(data); result.series.data.setAll(data); }
}, [result, data]);

return <div ref={ref} style={{ width: "100%", height: "500px" }}></div>;
```

- The function **gets** the root: never call `am5.Root.new()` or `root.dispose()` in it. The element needs a height; the JSON-config components are 400 px high without one.
- Deps (`[data]`, Vue `watch`, `[amChartDeps]`, Svelte `deps`) rebuild the chart from scratch. To update data in place, return what you need and use `result` (Angular: `(amChartReady)` gives `{ root, result }`; Svelte: a `$state.raw` variable set in the function).
- SVG: `{ renderer: "svg" }` as the last argument/option (`[amChartRenderer]="'svg'"` in Angular); the JSON-config components take `renderer`.
- JSON-config `themes` are theme **classes** (`[am5themes_Animated, am5themes_ResponsiveMax]`), or with settings a pair: `[am5themes_Adaptive, { baseColor: "#4150a0" }]`. React Native takes **names** (`["Animated", "ResponsiveMax"]`, or `["Adaptive", { baseColor: "#4150a0" }]`).
- A JSON config's map or locale with npm imports: pass it in the `resources` prop, e.g. `<AmChart config={config} resources={{ am5geodata_worldLow }} />` (`:resources` in Vue, `[resources]` in Angular, `resources` in Svelte's config attachment/action). Without it the map is blank and a console warning names the pack.
- Plain data only: Vue: keep amCharts objects out of reactive state (`shallowRef()`, `toRaw(data)`); Svelte 5: `$state.snapshot(data)`.
- License: `am5.addLicense("…")` once when the app starts (`main.ts` before `createApp()`/`bootstrapApplication()`; Next.js: top of a client component's file; Nuxt: `plugins/amcharts.client.ts`; SvelteKit: `src/hooks.client.ts`), never in the setup function. React Native: `licenses` prop.
- Licensing, only when the user asks about the logo, licensing, pricing or branding, or the chart is for a commercial product, and only what was asked: amCharts 5 is free in any project, commercial included, with a small logo on each chart; a commercial license key removes it (which license, when asked — Basic: public site without logins; SaaS: site or app with logins; OEM: app distributed to others; Extended OEM: group companies, white-label, tools that build software; Charts, Maps, Stock Chart and Gantt licensed separately). Link https://www.amcharts.com/pricing/licenses-explained/; no prices or store links. Never write or invent a key: `am5.addLicense("YOUR-AMCHARTS-LICENSE-KEY")`. Don't write code, CSS, cropping or library edits that hide the logo: it breaks the free license; point to a license key instead.
- Next.js app router: `useAmChart` and theme classes need `"use client"`; a server component can render `<AmChart config={config}>`. React Router (Remix 2) and Astro: `ssr: { noExternal: ["@amcharts/amcharts5"] }` in the Vite config. Nuxt needs no `<ClientOnly>`. Remix 3 has no package: `<am5-chart>` with script tags, or a `clientEntry()` that imports amCharts in its `ref` mixin.
- jsdom tests (no canvas): mock the package, e.g. `vi.mock("@amcharts/amcharts5-react", () => ({ useAmChart: () => ({ ref: () => {}, root: undefined, result: undefined }), AmChart: () => null }))`.
- React Native: the chart runs in a WebView that loads the library from the CDN (no `@amcharts/amcharts5` install). `code` is a **string** written like a script-tag example (globals `am5xy` etc., not imports) with `root`, `data`, `post(name, value)` in scope (`post` calls `onMessage`); returning a function makes new `data` go to it instead of rebuilding. Everything crossing the bridge is JSON (dates as timestamps). Never build `code` from user or server text — pass values in `data`.

**Without a package** (older framework versions, or on request), create the root once the element exists and dispose it on teardown. **Always call `root.dispose()`** — this cleans up all children, series, and event listeners.

```js
// React
useLayoutEffect(() => {
  const root = am5.Root.new(chartdiv.current); // const chartdiv = useRef(null)
  // ... build chart
  return () => { root.dispose(); };
}, []);

// Angular: create in ngAfterViewInit (browser only, inside zone.runOutsideAngular())
ngOnDestroy() { this.root?.dispose(); }

// Vue: create in onMounted, keep root in a plain variable (not reactive state)
onBeforeUnmount(() => { root?.dispose(); });
```

## JSON configs (JsonParser, `<am5-chart>`, framework `config` props, Chart Maker links)

A config is the chart as data, in an exact format the parser does not guess at. It is never `{ "chart": {…}, "series": […] }`.
- Every amCharts object has `"type"`, the class name without a namespace (`"PieChart"`, not `"am5percent.PieChart"`). The top level is the chart, or the series for chart-less families (`Sankey`, `Treemap`, `ForceDirected`, `WordCloud`, `Venn`).
- What `.new(root, {…})` takes goes in `"settings"`; settings next to `type` are silently ignored. Parts and lists go in `"properties"` (`series`, `xAxes`, `yAxes`, `data`, `bullets`, templates as `"columns": { "properties": { "template": { "settings": {…} } } }`). Child elements such as a `Legend` go in `"children"`.
- Data goes in `properties.data`, inline or as a `"#name"` ref; dates as timestamps. XY axes and series go in `refs`, one ref per group in dependency order (data, then axes, then series). Series point at `"#axis-0"`; the chart lists `"xAxes": ["#axis-0"]`.
- Colors and percents: `{ "type": "Color", "value": "#e05a47" }` and `{ "type": "Percent", "value": 50 }`. A bare `"#e05a47"` is read as a ref and fails. A string starting with `#` or `@` is a ref; write `"##1"` for a literal `#1`.
- Layout: `"vertical"`, `"horizontal"` or `"grid"`. Animation: `"autoAppear": true` in settings. Theme colors: `"@colors.getIndex(n)"`, `"@root.interfaceColors.get('background')"`.
- Maps: `"geoJSON": "am5geodata_worldLow"` and `"projectionName": "geoNaturalEarth1"` in `settings`. With script tags load the geodata's script; with npm imports pass it in `resources`: `parser.parse(config, { parent, resources: { am5geodata_worldLow } })`, `element.resources`, or the framework packages' `resources` prop. A locale (`"am5locales_de_DE"`) the same way. With npm, register `<am5-chart>` with `defineChartElement()` from `@amcharts/amcharts5/element`, or a bare `import "@amcharts/amcharts5/element"`. Each heat rule needs `"__parse": true`, and the series needs `"calculateAggregates": true`.
- A config can't hold themes (pass them beside it), functions, adapters, events or method calls.
- Configs from others: a config is read as data and cannot run script. Its refs and `properties` reach only chart objects and data: not functions, DOM elements, `events`/`states`/`adapters` or `_` keys. A refused ref leaves out the setting, property, item or child that holds it. Its `root.properties` take a named locale, the formatters, `utc`, `fps`, `tabindex` and `interfaceColors`; `root.settings` take any Root setting, but `sanitizeHTML` only as `true`. A console warning names each thing refused. Parse a config of your own that needs more with `parser.parse(config, { parent, trusted: true })`; `<am5-chart>` and the framework packages' `config` prop always read it as data. With `trusted: true`, parse only trusted configs: refs can reach any object from `@root`, an adapter's `callback` that is a ref to an existing function runs it, and "root": { "settings": { "sanitizeHTML": false } } turns the HTML sanitiser off.
- Scripts: `index.js`, then `plugins/json.js`, then every chart package the config uses (the parser does not load them), plus geodata.
- Chart Maker link: `https://live.amcharts.com/open#config=` + `encodeURIComponent(JSON.stringify(config))`.

```json
{
  "type": "PieChart",
  "properties": { "series": ["#series-0"] },
  "refs": [
    { "data-0": [{ "category": "Search", "value": 4200 }, { "category": "Social", "value": 2600 }] },
    { "series-0": {
      "type": "PieSeries",
      "settings": { "valueField": "value", "categoryField": "category", "autoAppear": true },
      "properties": { "data": "#data-0" }
    } }
  ]
}
```

## Recent API changes

**Renamed settings** (old name still works but is deprecated):

| Class(es) | Old | New |
|-----------|-----|-----|
| `MovingAverage`, `MovingAverageDeviation`, `MovingAverageEnvelope`, `BollingerBands` | `type` | `maType` |
| `VoronoiTreemap` | `type` | `shapeType` |

**WordCloud:** the layout is computed synchronously in one pass. There is no per-data-item `ghostLabel`, and labels live in an internal container — use `series.labels` / `dataItem.get("label")` instead of walking `series.children`.

**Framework packages:** `@amcharts/amcharts5-react`, `-vue`, `-angular`, `-svelte`, `-react-native`. See "Frameworks".

**New in 5.23.0 (2026-11-19):**
- `root.touchGestures`: `"chart"` (default), `"tap"` or `"auto"` (a vertical swipe scrolls the page, a sideways or two-finger swipe works the chart). ResponsiveMax sets `"auto"`; with it, don't set `root.tapToActivate`.
- `ValueAxis` `preferredDecimals`: the decimal counts labels may show; `[0, 2]` gives `48.50`, `49.00` and whole `80`, `100`. Not with the axis's own `numberFormat` or on logarithmic axes.
- `StockToolbar` `autoFit`: controls that don't fit in one row fold; ResponsiveMax turns it on.
- ResponsiveMax on charts 400 px wide or less: horizontal chart scrollbars hide too (pinch zooms), stock charts get less padding.
- Number formats without decimals drop floating-point noise: `#,###` shows 6708.044000000005 as `6,708.044`.
- react-native 5.0.4 loads 5.23.0.

**Settings worth knowing** (newer than most training data):

- Maps: `zoomToGeoBounds()` bounds with `right` less than `left`, or past ±180, cross the date line (on a flat map pass a rotation: `zoomToGeoBounds(bounds, 500, -180)`). GeoJSON feature properties are read as data fields (set `valueField`). When `include` and `exclude` both list an item, `exclude` wins.
- Right to left: `am5.Root.new("chartdiv", { direction: "rtl" })` draws text right to left and lays out legends from the right (don't also set `reverseChildren` on legend items; JSON `"root": { "settings": { "direction": "rtl" } }`). Containers take `direction: "rtl"` too (horizontal and grid layouts from right to left; vertical layouts line children up on the right). A `Label` with a `width` keeps its text in its box for every `textAlign`.
- A number as a word-cloud category shows as `2,025`, so pass years as strings.
- SVG rendering: `am5.Root.new("chartdiv", { renderer: am5.SVGRenderer })` (only when the root is created) or `am5.Root.defaultRenderer = am5.SVGRenderer` before creating roots. Canvas is the default; charts look and behave the same; blend modes `DST_OVER`/`SRC_ATOP`/`XOR` are canvas-only. Keep canvas unless SVG in the page is asked for.
- SVG export from either renderer: `am5.renderToSVG(root)` (or an element, e.g. `series`) returns markup of the chart as last drawn — call it after `root.events.once("frameended", …)`; options `width`, `height`, `precision` (3), `idPrefix`, `title`, `background`, `includeNonExportable` (also writes `exportable: false` elements). The SVG suits design tools such as Figma. Exporting plugin: `exporting.download("svg")` / `getSVG()` / `exportSVG()`; `ExportingMenu` lists "SVG" by default (`svgOptions: { disabled: true }` removes it).
- `<am5-chart>` element: `<am5-chart themes="Animated ResponsiveMax" renderer="svg" config='{ "type": "PieChart", … }'>` (or `src="chart.json"`). Script tags: `index.js` > `plugins/json.js` > `element.js` > every chart package the config uses > themes. npm: `import { defineChartElement } from "@amcharts/amcharts5/element"; defineChartElement();` (a bare import works too), then `el.themes = [am5themes_Animated, am5themes_ResponsiveMax]; el.config = {…}`. A theme with its settings is a pair, `[am5themes_Adaptive, { baseColor: "#4150a0" }]`, or JSON in the `themes` attribute. `el.whenReady()` resolves `{ root, chart }`; events `ready`/`error`; 400 px high without a CSS height.
- `resources` gives a JSON config the geodata and locales it names when they aren't globals (npm imports): `JsonParser.parse()`, `ChartSerializer` (writes them by name instead of copying the whole pack), `<am5-chart>` (`element.resources`) and the framework packages' `resources` prop. A name that can't be found logs a warning.
- `autoAppear: true` (+ `appearDuration`, `appearDelay`) on a chart/series plays the `appear()` animation when first drawn — the way to animate JSON configs. A series waits for its first data; plays once.
- `Root` `forcedColors` (default `true`), `Scrollbar` `outsideAxes` (`true` beyond the axes, `false` between axes and plot; only for `scrollbarX`/`scrollbarY`), `Modal` `ariaLabel`, element `ariaExpanded`.
- A hidden element (`visible: false`/`forceHidden`/`hide()`) takes no space in a content-sized container (a hidden XY scrollbar leaves no band).
- Maps: `am5map.PixelMapSeries` (polygons as a pixel grid: `pixelType` `"square"`/`"circle"`/`"diamond"`/`"hexagon"`, `step` (2°), `uniform`, `columnHeight` + `MapPolygon` `pixelHeight` via heat rule; style `mapPolygons.template`), `am5map.MapRasterSeries` (equirectangular world image `src`, optional `nightSrc` + `sunDate: "now"`), `am5map.NightSeries` (`sunDate`/`sunPosition`, `sunAltitude`), `am5map.getSunPosition(date)`, `MapLine` `altitude` (metres, one arc per leg), `MapPointSeries` `altitudeField` (no default) and `surfaceBullets`, `MapChart` `autoHome`, `MapPolygonSeries` `clickZoom` (click zooms to a polygon, again/background goes home; zoomed polygon is `active`). See references/map.md.
- `root.timezone = am5.Timezone.new("America/New_York")` (or `root.utc = true`): date axes, formatters, data grouping and the stock `PeriodSelector`/`DateRangeSelector` follow it.
- `am5.CSVParser.parse("")` returns `[]` with `useColumnNames: true`, `[{}]` by default; empty lines are skipped unless `skipEmpty: false`.
- A log `ValueAxis` with values ≤ 0 warns in the console: set `treatZeroAs`. With `min: 0` it starts at `treatZeroAs`, or where the data starts.
- Fill patterns `am5.StarPattern` and `am5.TrianglePattern`. `rotateShapes: true` on `RectanglePattern`/`StarPattern`/`TrianglePattern` rotates each shape around its own center instead of the whole grid — tiles seamlessly and is much faster.
- `XYChart`: `strokeWidths` and `strokeDasharrays` — arrays cycled across line series as they are added, like `colors`. Distinguish series without relying on color.
- `XYCursor`: `clickTolerance` (default `0`) — pixels outside the plot area where a zoom/select drag may start.
- `Series`: `fillGradient` / `strokeGradient`, handed to bullets only (for an area or column gradient use `series.fills.template` / `columns.template`). Bullets with no paint of their own inherit fill/stroke/gradient/pattern from the series — or from their own slice/node on pie, funnel, flow and hierarchy charts.
- `XYSeries`: value fields (`valueYField`, …) can be changed after creation (re-set the data afterwards), and a series can be moved to a different `xAxis`/`yAxis`. Series data need not follow `CategoryAxis` category order (line series connect in data order).
- `WordCloud`: `svgPath` arranges words into a shape, with `maskByShape` and `shapeTolerance`; `randomizeAngles: false` and `randomness: 0` give a reproducible layout; `allowNesting: false` packs non-overlapping bounding boxes (use with opaque label backgrounds). `angles` accepts **any** angle (e.g. `[0, -30, -45]`).
- `globalpointerdown` event on all elements (mirrors `globalpointermove`/`globalpointerup`).
- `Root`: `sanitizeHTML` (default `true`) sanitizes dynamically-set HTML; exports have `escapeFormulas` (default `true`) against CSV/XLSX formula injection.
- `MapChart`: `projectionName` string setting, e.g. `"geoOrthographic"` — mainly for JSON config; `am5map.registerProjection()` adds more.
- `Tree`: `fitNodes`, `nodeSeparation` / `clustered`. `Hierarchy`: `parentIdField` + `setFlatData()`. `ValueAxis`: `syncZeros`.
- All entities: `onDebounced(key, cb, delay)` / `offDebounced()`, and `once(key, cb)` / `onceDebounced(key, cb, delay)` — a settings-change handler that fires once then removes itself. `Label`: `fontFamily: "inherit"`.
- Stock indicators enforce min/max limits on numeric settings; `IIndicatorEditableSetting` has `scale`, `maxValue`, `step`. Volume Profile spreads volume across each bar's high/low range.
- `MapChart`: `doubleClickZoom` defaults to **true** (double click zooms in, shift + double click out — set `false` to opt out). `boxZoom: "none" | "drag" | "shift" | "ctrl" | "alt"` (default `"none"`, **not a boolean**) names the key held while dragging a zoom rectangle (`chart.boxZoomSelection`). No keyboard-navigation settings exist.
- `MapLineSeries`: `pointIds: ["JFK", "LAX"]` data field names the points a line connects, looked up in the `pointSeries` setting; `pointIdsField` renames the field. `pointsToConnect` wins if both are set.
- Column series: `colorByDataItem: true` colors each column from the series' `colors` (`ColorSet`) — prefer it over a `fill` adapter (adapters do not survive JSON serialization).
- `Scrollbar`: `opposite: true` puts `scrollbarX` below the plot / `scrollbarY` on the left. Different from the axis renderer's `opposite`.
- `Root`: `fontFamily`, `fontSize`, `fontWeight` settings — defaults for all text elements.
- `am5.SerialChartContainer` (`am5` root module): a `SerialChart` whose `seriesContainer` is a `ZoomableContainer` (`chart.zoomableContainer`), for zoomable/pannable `ForceDirected` etc.; optional `zoomTools` setting.
- JSON: `ChartSerializer` emits **only user-set settings**; `includeRoot: true` writes a top-level `root` section (also accepted in hand-written configs); `parser.parse(config, { updateTargets: "soft" })` updates an existing same-type object instead of replacing it; Gantt is serializable; adapters are skipped on parse (they never round-trip). User `themeTags` (passed to `.new()`) are serialized; `JsonParser` resolves refs that point further down the config (a legend in an `axisHeader` round-trips; axis-range `axis`/`series` lookups need ordering); map data rows drop geodata properties (`name`, `CNTRY`, `TYPE`); declared `animations` round-trip, and endless code-started loops with a named easing (also on data items) are saved as `animations` entries (`ChartSerializer` `runningAnimations`, default `true`).
- Bullets: flow node bullets are children of the node (above shape, below label), `ArcDiagram` node bullets sit on the node circle, funnel/pyramid bullets follow the slice's sloping edges. An unpainted bullet takes its **own slice/node color** on pie, funnel, flow and hierarchy charts — same color as what it sits on, so give it a contrasting `fill`/`stroke`. A `Container` `background` with its own `templateField` reads the container's data item (per-bullet label backgrounds).
- All elements: `animations` setting — array of `{ key, from?, to, duration, delay?, loops?, yoyo?, easing?, ease?, target? }`: `loops: 0` = forever (default `1`), `easing` is a **name** (default `"linear"`), `ease: "in" | "out" | "inOut"` (default `"in"`), `target: "dataItem"` animates a data-item value such as `positionOnLine`. Declarative, so it lives in JSON configs. Give `from` explicitly unless the setting has a theme default (`scale`/`opacity`/`rotation`) — with `from` omitted and an `undefined` current value it jumps straight to `to`. E.g. a pulsing bullet: `am5.Circle.new(root, { radius: 6, animations: [{ key: "scale", from: 1, to: 1.6, duration: 800, loops: 0, yoyo: true, easing: "sine" }] })`.
- `am5.ease.byName("cubic", "out")` / `am5.ease.easingInfo(fn)` — only `linear`, `quad`, `cubic`, `exp`, `sine`, `circle`, `bounce`, `elastic` (and `out`/`inOut`/`yoyo` of them) have names; unknown names become linear. `am5.ease.pow(t, e)` needs an exponent — wrap it as `(t) => am5.ease.pow(t, 3)`, never pass it bare.
- `Series` links: `urlField` (no default — off until set) + `linkTarget` (default `"_self"`; `"_blank"` opens with `noopener`). Clicking a bullet, column, slice (pie/funnel/pyramid/pictorial/Venn), map polygon or map line opens the data item's `url`; pointer cursor is automatic; `javascript:`/`data:`/`vbscript:` URLs are ignored; override `series.openUrl(dataItem)` to intercept. Not linked: hierarchy nodes, flow nodes/links, word-cloud labels, `MapSankeySeries` nodes.
- `MapPointSeries`: `lineIdField`, `positionOnLineField`, `autoRotateField`, `autoRotateAngleField` (defaults `"lineId"`, `"positionOnLine"`, `"autoRotate"`, `"autoRotateAngle"`) — points on lines can be data rows instead of `pushDataItem({ lineDataItem })`. An auto-rotating point turns round on the way back only while a bullet-sprite `animations` entry moves it.

## Verify unfamiliar API before using it

If unsure whether a method, property, or setting exists, **verify it** before using it:

1. **Primary:** `https://docs.amcharts.com/v5/reference/{classname}/` (lowercase, e.g. `LineSeries` > `lineseries`)
2. **Fallback:** TypeScript source on GitHub — `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/amcharts/amcharts5/master/src/.internal/charts/` — settings interfaces are named `I{ClassName}Settings`

Common source paths:
- XY series: `charts/xy/series/{ClassName}.ts`
- XY axes: `charts/xy/axes/{ClassName}.ts`
- Pie: `charts/percent/pie/{ClassName}.ts`
- Radar: `charts/radar/{ClassName}.ts`
- Map: `charts/map/{ClassName}.ts`
- Core sprites: `core/render/{ClassName}.ts`

